  "id": "Compound::DB00514 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Dextromethorphan exerts its pharmacological effects through a series of mechanistic interactions that ultimately involve the cytochrome P450 3A4 (Cyp3a4) enzyme. The evidence suggests that Dextromethorphan binds to Cyp2b6 and Cyp2e1, which are both involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics and certain drugs, respectively. These enzymes then participate in metabolic pathways that are ultimately linked to Cyp3a4. The observed pathway links Dextromethorphan to Cyp3a4 through a chain of enzymatic activities, where the metabolic processes initiated by Cyp2b6 and Cyp2e1 are indirectly associated with Cyp3a4. This suggests that Dextromethorphan may influence Cyp3a4 through a metabolic cascade, although the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp3a4 in the metabolism of xenobiotics, and the potential for Dextromethorphan to modulate this process.",
